	doi = {10.1109/TED.2025.3626326},
	abstract = {In this work, a novel vertical gate-all-around field-effect transistor (VGAAFET) structure is proposed for scaling CMOS technology. Compared to the traditional VGAAFET, the lengths of gate (Lg), spacer (L \_{\textbackslash}text sp ), and source/drain (L \_{\textbackslash}text S/{\textbackslash}text D ) are predefined by the Si/SiGe/Si/SiGe/Si epitaxial stacks. Benefiting from the decoupling of the Lg, L \_{\textbackslash}text sp , and L \_{\textbackslash}text S/{\textbackslash}text D from the contact gate pitch (CGP) in the VGAAFET, the Lg and L \_{\textbackslash}text sp have been optimized to enhance the device performance without extending the footprint. To address the structural asymmetry and reduce the parasitic resistance (R \_{\textbackslash}text para ) of the VGAAFET, the backside contacts (BSCs) technology is integrated. Compared to the frontside contacts (FSCs) VGAAFET, the bottom source/drain resistance (R \_{\textbackslash}text BotS/{\textbackslash}text D ) is reduced by 46.5\%, and the on-state normalized current (I \_{\textbackslash}text on,{\textbackslash}text norm ) is increased by 21.8\% for BSC-VGAAFET. Additionally, by employing the extension region doping (ERD) technology to improve the electrical characteristics symmetry between n/p VGAAFETs, an enhanced n/p current ratio from 1.31 to 1.16 has been achieved. Furthermore, to benchmark the power, performance, and area (PPA) characteristics between the VGAAFET and lateral GAAFET (LGAAFET) at the circuit-level, the Nand2 standard cells are designed at the same footprint, and evaluated in our design technology co-optimization (DTCO) platform. The results of the 15-stage ring oscillator (RO) demonstrate that at the same supply voltage (V \_{\textbackslash}text dd ) and footprint, the BSC-VGAAFET achieves 52.2\% frequency improvement and 21.6\% energy-delay product (EDP) reduction compared to the LGAAFET. Therefore, the BSC-VGAAFET is a promising transistor architecture for next-generation integrated circuits (ICs).},
